From: SmartWRT
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: keep the link frequency at a background CAC

nl80211_start_radar_detection() stores the frequency of the CAC as the
frequency of the link, which send_mlme uses for a frame that comes
without one. A background CAC leaves the AP on its operating channel, so
each Probe, Authentication and Association Response then went out with
the frequency of the CAC, and mac80211 refused it with -EBUSY as an
off-channel frame. hostapd logged "handle_probe_req: send failed" and
"send_auth_reply: send failed" until the next beacon update, which sets
the frequency of the link back.

The generic background radar flow sets the channel of the AP after it
starts the CAC, which hides this. The staged zero-wait DFS flow starts
the CAC with the AP already up, also again after radar, the end of the
NOP and an abort.

Keep the frequency of the link where the CAC runs on the background
chain.
---
--- a/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
+++ b/src/drivers/driver_nl80211.c
@@ -11742,7 +11742,12 @@ static int nl80211_start_radar_detection
 
 	ret = send_and_recv_cmd(drv, msg);
 	if (ret == 0) {
-		nl80211_link_set_freq(bss, freq->link_id, freq->freq);
+		/* A background CAC leaves the AP on its operating channel,
+		 * which send_mlme takes from the link for a frame without
+		 * a frequency. */
+		if (!freq->radar_background)
+			nl80211_link_set_freq(bss, freq->link_id,
+					      freq->freq);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
